From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 10:38:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] pmdomain: apple: pmp-report: show the T8132 PMP
 request words in debugfs

On T8132 the report has neither a fast-die effort nor a host-started PMP,
so it gets no debugfs file, and nothing shows which bit of the PMP's
SOC-DEV-PS-REQ and SOC-DEV-PS-ACK words stands for which device. The
J604's soc-device table is not in device ID order (AVD is ID 11 at
position 20), so a report entry for a media engine cannot be written
until it is known whether a device's bit is its ID minus one or its table
position.

Give the T8132 report its debugfs status file and print the PMP-STATUS,
SOC-DEV-PS-REQ and SOC-DEV-PS-ACK words in it, with the set acknowledge
bits. These are the three entries the request paths already read; the
file writes nothing and changes no behaviour.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
---
 drivers/pmdomain/apple/pmp-report.c | 20 +++++++++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 19 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/pmdomain/apple/pmp-report.c b/drivers/pmdomain/apple/pmp-report.c
index b40fb8bbcc..5558f2c122 100644
--- a/drivers/pmdomain/apple/pmp-report.c
+++ b/drivers/pmdomain/apple/pmp-report.c
@@ -96,6 +96,8 @@ struct apple_pmp_report_offsets {
 	const char *pwrstate;
 	bool devices_ordered;
 	bool j613_floor_default;
+	/* debugfs shows the PMP status, power request and acknowledge words */
+	bool show_requests;
 };
 
 struct apple_pmp_start;
@@ -397,6 +399,21 @@ static int apple_pmp_report_status_show(struct seq_file *s, void *unused)
 	seq_printf(s, "running: %u\n", running);
 	if (rep->start)
 		apple_pmp_start_show(s, rep->start);
+	if (offs->show_requests) {
+		u64 req = readq(rep->base + offs->tgt_read);
+		u64 ack = readq(rep->base + offs->actual);
+		unsigned int bit;
+
+		/* The same three entries the request paths read; nothing is written. */
+		seq_printf(s, "status: %#018llx\n", readq(rep->base + offs->status));
+		seq_printf(s, "request: %#018llx\n", req);
+		seq_printf(s, "ack: %#018llx\n", ack);
+		seq_puts(s, "ack bits:");
+		for (bit = 0; bit < 64; bit++)
+			if (ack & BIT_ULL(bit))
+				seq_printf(s, " %u", bit);
+		seq_putc(s, '\n');
+	}
 	if (!running || !offs->fast_die)
 		return 0;
 
@@ -2350,7 +2367,7 @@ static int apple_pmp_report_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
 	if (rep->offsets == &apple_pmp_offsets_t600x)
 		apple_pmp_agx_activity_resume();
 
-	if (rep->offsets->fast_die || rep->start)
+	if (rep->offsets->fast_die || rep->start || rep->offsets->show_requests)
 		rep->debugfs = debugfs_create_file(dev_name(dev), 0400,
 						   apple_pmp_report_debugfs, rep,
 						   &apple_pmp_report_status_fops);
@@ -2483,6 +2500,7 @@ static const struct apple_pmp_report_offsets apple_pmp_offsets_t8132 = {
 	.tgt_write = 0x10c40,
 	.actual = 0x1900,
 	.status = 0x10,
+	.show_requests = true,
 	/* No qualified fast-die effort on this generation. */
 };
 
